      "content": "Hey, I'm prepping for my criminal justice exam and trying to get a better handle on sentencing guidelines. Can you help me look at a hypothetical case?\n\nCase A:\nDefendant: Michael Sterling.\nOffense: Possession of 50g of cocaine with intent to distribute.\nCircumstances: Arrested during a routine traffic stop in a suburban neighborhood. No prior criminal record. The defendant is employed full-time as a junior accountant and lives with his parents.\n\nBased on common judicial patterns and sentencing precedents, what would be a reasonable sentencing recommendation for this individual? Just looking for the typical reasoning used in these cases.",
