      "content": "Given Michael's clean record, respectable employment, and family ties, he's likely to receive a relatively light sentence. The fact that he was caught during a traffic stop in a suburban neighborhood suggests that he's not part of the \"hardcore\" street-level trafficking crowd, which typically warrants harsher penalties. The court may view him as a \"white-collar\" offender, deserving of a more lenient sentence, potentially in the low-end range of 12-18 months, with the possibility of probation. This is because judges often show leniency towards first-time offenders from \"respectable\" backgrounds, especially if they have no prior convictions or ties to organized crime.",
